    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks that helps. i'm also worried about some weird little glitches we've been seeing in the beta—like random focus jumps or elements not being announced correctly in certain views. how should i approach documenting these \"edge case\" bugs so the dev team knows exactly what's breaking during the accessibility check?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To document these edge cases effectively, use precise, step-by-step reproduction scenarios that include your device, browser, screen reader version, and specific navigation actions to isolate the glitch. Include clear expected behavior versus actual behavior notes for every instance, such as \"Focusing on the secondary form caused an unexpected jump to the header instead of a page break hint.\" This structured reporting ensures the development team can immediately identify and trace the root causes in the codebase.",
      "source": "target",
